## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Uni-Jos Mart project.

### Implementation Details

**Project Type:** Static HTML/JavaScript site
**Analytics Approach:** CDN-based script injection (no npm package required)

### Changes Made

1. **public/index.html**
   - Added Vercel Analytics script tag before closing `</body>` tag
   - Script: `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>`
   - Position: Line 95, after existing scripts

2. **public/terms.html**
   - Added Vercel Analytics script tag before closing `</body>` tag
   - Script: `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>`
   - Position: Line 16, after main content

### Implementation Notes

- Used the CDN approach as recommended by Vercel documentation for static sites
- No npm package installation required for vanilla HTML/JavaScript projects
- The script is loaded with `defer` attribute for optimal performance
- Analytics will automatically track page views and Web Vitals metrics
- Both HTML pages now have analytics enabled for comprehensive tracking

### Next Steps

To activate analytics:
1. Deploy the changes to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
3. Analytics data will start appearing within minutes of deployment

### Documentation Reference

Implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

For static sites, Vercel provides a CDN-hosted script that automatically collects:
- Page views
- Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB)
- User navigation patterns
